rem$ CONDENSED KEY TO POLYPORACEAE AND POROID GENERA OF OTHER FAMILlES 
The numbers in bold refer to the main key, those in normal print refer to the condensed key. 
1,11$ Basidiocarp more or less centrally stipitate (all species with numerous pilei from a common base belong here) 
1,2$ Basidiocarp resupinate to pileate, sometimes with a tapering lateraI base or stipe
2,22$ Hymenophore hydnoid, lamellate, daedaleoid to sinuous 
2,3$ Hymenophore with angular to round pores, sometimes slightly split and dentate in the dissepiments 
3,30$ Spores omamented
3,4$ Spores smooth  
4,35$ Spores, cystidia or hyphae amyloid or dextrinoid
4,5$ No amyloid or dextrinoid reaction in spores, cystidia or hyphae
5,41$Generative hyphae with simple septa 
5,6$Generative hyphae with clamps 
