24,0$Pileus semi glossy and smooth, faintly zoned; hymenophore lamellate to sinuous; context sepia brown; spores 7-11µm  long ; causes a white rot $Daedaleopsis
24,0$Pileus dull, finely velutinate to irregularly tufted, mostly azonate, hymenophore daedaleoid to sinuous, context tan to ochraceous; spores 5,5-7µm long, usually very difficult to find in dry specimens; causes a brown rot $Daedalea
25,0$Generative hyphae with simple septa; skeletocystidia present . $Irpex lacteus
25,26$Generative hyphae with clamps; skeletocystidia absent; hymenial cystidia absent or present
26,0$Hyphal system monomitic $Spongipellis
