rem$ Basidiocarps sessile to resupinate; hymenophore poroid; spores smooth; spores, cystidia and hyphae amyloid or dextrinoid in Melzer's reagent( Spores, cystidia or hyphae without reaction in Melzer's reagent, see 31)
35,0$Spores amyloid $Anomoporia
35,36$Spores dextrinoid or negative in Melzer's reagent
36,0$Cystidia present and amyloid $Amylocystis
36,37$Cystidia absent
37,0$Hyphal system monomitic with clamped hyphae; spores cylindrical, dextrinoid . $Parmastomyces
37,38$Hyphal system di-to trimitic; generative hyphae with clamps or simple septa; spores globose, ellipsoid to truncate, dextrinoid to non-dextrinoid
