59,0$Basidiocarp soft and flexible; spores cylindrical; causes a brown rot $Gloeophyllum
60,61$Context dark umber brown and separated from persistent or transient tomentum by a black zone, which by age may become a thin black cuticle; basidiocarps effused reflexed or pileate; binding hyphae usually rare or absent; spores usually shorter than 12 µm 
60,62$Context mostly in shades of rusty to umber brown, tomentum if present, often villose to strigose, not separated from context by black zone; if pileus smooth, then grey to pale brown; binding hyphae in context; spores longer than 12 µm 
