' Basidiocarps sessile to resupinate; hymenophore poroid; spores smooth; all structures negative in Melzer's reagent; generative hyphae with clamps; context and tubes light-coloured; cystidia present in hymenium or context (Cystidia absent from hymenium or context, see 65)
64,65$Hyphal system dimitic with skeletal hyphae; pore surface pinkish, cocoa-coloured, yellow to pale brown or violet
64,67$Hyphal system monomitic; pore surface white to discoloured sordid ochraceous when dry
65,0$Basidiocarp pileate; pileus grey to ochraceous or white; pore surface often with violet shades when fresh, spores cylindrical, longer than 7 µm $Trichaptum
65,66$Basidiocarp resupinate to rarely pileate; pore surface cocoa-brown, pinkish to yellow; spores shorter than 7 µm 
66,0$Cystidia large and ventricose; skeletal hyphae few, restricted to the context; pore surface yellow; causes a brown rot $Auriporia aurolenta
66,0$Cystidia club shaped, formed by the outer encrusted parts of skeletal hyphae; skeletal hyphae dominating; pore surface cocoa-brown, pinkish to pale straw-coloured; causes a white rot $Junghuhnia
67,0$Basidiocarp large and sappy; upper surface hirsute; cystidia ventricose, up to 50µm  long $Climacocystis
67,68$Basidiocarp resupinate to pileate, tough to soft; pileus if present, smooth or finely velutinate; cystidia ventricose to tubular 
68,0$Cystidia tubular, thin-walled and smooth; spores allantoid, 3-4 µm long; causes a white rot $Chaetoporellus
68,0$Cystidia clavated to ventricose, apically encrusted and thick-walled; spores cylindrical to allantoid, longer than 4 µm ; causes a brown rot $Oligoporus

'Basidiocarps sessile to resupinate; hymenophore poroid; spores smooth; spores, cystidia and hyphae negative in Melzer's reagent; generative hyphae with clamps; tubes and context light-coloured; cystidia absent; hyphal system monomitic. (Hyphal system di-or trimitic, see 75)
69,70$Basidiocarps resupinate
