72,0$Basidiocarp resupinate; causing a white rot $Ceriporiopsis
72,0$Basidiocarp resupinate to pileate; causing a brown rot $Oligoporus
73,0$Spores drop-shaped to globose, thick-walled and cyanophilous $Spongipellis
73,74$Spores differently shaped, thin-walled and non-cyanophilous
74,0$Pileus adpressed velutinate and dark brown or glabrous with a black, in part velutinous wrinkled surface; pores and tubes whitish to pale brown when fresh $Ischnoderma
74,75$Pileus white, greyish 10 discoloured, but never with a black wrinkled surface 
75,0$Tube layer buff, grey to blackish; context white; in one species separated from tubes by a thin dark zone, causing a white rot $Bjerkandera
75,76$Tubes and context more or less of same colour, or tubes at least not grey to almost black, no distinct dense zone between context and tubes
